INSERT INTO characters (slug,name,team,creator,owner_id,tags,appears_in,data,status,url_slug,created_at,updated_at) VALUES
('colossus','Colossus','outsider','Goodpart',NULL,NULL,'The Menagerie','{"slug":"colossus","name":"Colossus","team":"outsider","ability":"You might not die if executed. Your neighbours might register as a Colossus of your alignment.","creator":"Goodpart","appearsIn":"The Menagerie","quote":"No. Weather is same up here. Yes. Doorway is hard.","lede":"The Colossus is so large they cover their neighbours, making them look like the Colossus too - for better or worse.","howToRun":["Be judicious with misregistration when it comes to the Colossus. Its ability can be extremely detrimental to town, so turning it off when necessary, or simply allowing the Colossus to die if executed, can ensure games remain in balance. Remember that while neighbours of the Colossus may register as the Colossus, they don''t have its ability: so if they are executed, unless otherwise stated, they die as normal.","Characters that rely on Outsiders as part of their ability, such as the No Dashii or Godfather, should interact with the Colossus, but again, use discretion so as not to tip the game too far in evil''s favour."],"tips":["The hulking Colossus is so large it can cause its neighbours to register as the Colossus as well. If you think it''s safe, let them know. But understand that trust in your neighbours can only go so far. Given that you are an Outsider, and your neighbours may register as the same, they are prime targets for a Fang Gu, Godfather, or any other evil that interacts with Outsiders. Are you covering for evil by having them register as a good Colossus? Are you causing No Dashii poisoning to spread farther than it reasonably could? Or are you doing nothing at all? It''s hard to say, but information around town should feel a little \"off\" with you around. Try to pinpoint how, and why, to help solve the game. If you''re convinced it''s safe to do so, consider requesting execution to lift the veil from your neighbours."],"bluffing":["While this may be tricky without characters like the Devil''s Advocate or Lleech in play, you can certainly bluff as the Colossus by playing around its strengths, in terms of how it can aid the evil team. Convincing town that you are the Colossus may mean that your neighbours draw undue suspicion, as your \"ability\" may be covering them. Poisoning confirmation roles like the Undertaker upon the execution of your neighbours can help to give you the social credit that you need to operate, so evaluate the tools at your disposal, and make them work if you can."],"fighting":[],"examples":["Jack is the Colossus. His neighbours are the Baron and the Empath. The Baron registers as a good Colossus until Jack''s death, causing the Tea Lady next to the Baron to believe that they are confirmed as good.","Emily is the Lleech claiming to be the Colossus. She is executed on Day 2 and does not die. She has Lleech hosted the Dreamer, who sees Emily''s neighbour as the Colossus or the Wraith, and Emily''s other neighbour as the Colossus or the Harpy."],"firstNight":0,"firstNightReminder":"","otherNight":0,"otherNightReminder":"","reminders":["Colossus","Colossus"],"setup":false,"image":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/colg.png","curata":false,"imageAlt":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/cole.png"}','published','the-menagerie/colossus',datetime('now'),datetime('now')),
('eccentric','Eccentric','outsider','Goodpart',NULL,NULL,'The Menagerie','{"slug":"eccentric","name":"Eccentric","team":"outsider","ability":"If you are nominated by evil and executed, your team loses. Anyone ''mad'' that you are in play might die. You cannot self-nominate. [Your token is a square]","creator":"Goodpart","appearsIn":"The Menagerie","quote":"Up is down! Left is right! Day is night! I am not me! I am you! Or are you me? Wait, I''m me? Round and round we go... Oh ho!","lede":"The Eccentric''s unique token means its presence is known to many, but mentioned by none.","howToRun":["In order to run this character online, you must include the Gardener Loric. On Night 1, before passing out tokens, wake each player clockwise and let them know the Eccentric''s token is, or is not in the bag, and ask whether they wish to take the token if so."],"tips":["Congratulations on being brave (or silly) enough to take the Eccentric''s token! Its unique shape in the bag means that anyone who drew a character before you knows you''re in play, and anyone after you doesn''t. Of course, no-one will be able to say so, because to do so risks an early exit, so play it cool, give nothing away until you''re dead, and let town tie itself in knots to work out whether you''re real or not.","Speaking of death, aside from dying at night, you''ll need to contend with nominations; the Eccentric must be nominated and executed by a good player, else they risk losing the game for their team, so if you''ve been framed, make sure the people pushing on you are backed up with information confirming them as good. If not, it''s time to fight like hell to clear your name, because you''re only a few votes away from an early loss.","On the upside, if you die by execution and the game continues, you can be reasonably certain your nominator is good, so speak with them and let them know!"],"bluffing":["While not impossible, the Eccentric''s square token gives away its presence readily. But don''t fret: if you''re the first to take a token, don''t feel the Eccentric in the bag, and draw an evil token, you''ve got a guaranteed bluff ready to go. Just be sure that the Outsider count checks out, and that you''re prepared for what comes when someone invokes your name and doesn''t die. It''s a \"might\", after all.","Play it as you would if good, be prepared to be framed, and if it''s time to go, insist that a teammate be the one to nominate you to help sell them as good. Insist that you live on days you''re nominated by players you wish to frame, but don''t let them know why! If you''ve got a Witch or Harpy handy, it may be worth coordinating your actions to \"confirm\" your role."],"fighting":[],"examples":["Zoe is the fourth player to take tokens this game, and decides to take the Eccentric''s token. Three people know the Eccentric is in play other than Zoe, so Zoe double claims one of them to infer, without alluding to her real role, that she may be the Eccentric.","Yang is the first player to take tokens this game, and does not feel the Eccentric''s token in the bag. They grab a token, receiving the Witch. They curse the town''s Savant, and heavily imply they are the Eccentric. The Savant believes Yang is the Eccentric and mistakenly mentions it: they nominate Yang, and die."],"firstNight":0,"firstNightReminder":"","otherNight":0,"otherNightReminder":"","reminders":[],"setup":false,"jinxes":[{"name":"Lycanthrope","align":"good","text":"The Faux Paw nominating the Eccentric does not trigger the Eccentric''s ability.","id":"lycanthrope"},{"name":"Spy","align":"good","text":"If the Spy and the Eccentric is in play, the Eccentric is drunk.","id":"spy"},{"name":"Widow","align":"good","text":"If the Widow and the Eccentric is in play, the Eccentric is drunk.","id":"widow"}],"image":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/eccg.png","curata":false,"imageAlt":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/ecce.png"}','published','the-menagerie/eccentric',datetime('now'),datetime('now')),
('egotist','Egotist','outsider','Goodpart',NULL,NULL,'The Menagerie','{"slug":"egotist","name":"Egotist","team":"outsider","ability":"One Townsfolk player who nominates you or votes on your execution is drunk until dawn, even if you are dead. You cannot self-nominate.","creator":"Goodpart","appearsIn":"The Menagerie","quote":"How dare you? I''ll have you know I am good friends with Baron Morozov - VERY good friends - and he can have you hanged for this. Who do you think you are? You know, you''re awfully talkative for a lowly librarian. I bet you don''t even read books. I''ve read over a hundred. Not to mention--","lede":"The Egotist drunks and befuddles those who would dare to nominate them.","howToRun":["Evil players can also be made drunk via the Egotist''s ability. Make sure to mark players as drunk immediately after the nomination commences in case they are a waking ability like the Slayer, Artist, etc.","As with the Butler or Golem, there is no penalty per se to self-nominating, but remind the Egotist that they cannot to ensure it doesn''t happen again."],"tips":["As an Outsider, it''s likely you''ll want out of town, and quickly - but your ability means that you are a liability. If you''re nominated, it may be worth trying to rally votes to ensure the damage you deal is as little as possible, but let town know of the damage nonetheless. If possible, try to rally Outsiders to vote on your execution, and hope that evil players join in, or ask spent roles that don''t mind being made drunk to stack on the votes. This should mitigate the worst of your ability, and ensure town''s information is as sound as possible."],"bluffing":["Bluffing as the Egotist, while possible, is difficult, because you run the risk of town wanting you out ASAP. With that said, the threat of being made drunk might be enough to persuade people not to nominate or vote on your execution. If you have a Poisoner or Lady Lace in your arsenal, you can simulate the Egotist''s ability by poisoning a player that was involved in a claimed Egotist vote. So let your bluff be your shield that protects you from execution!"],"fighting":[],"examples":["Andre is the Egotist. The Artist nominates them on Day 1. They are immediately drunk, and their Artist question yields arbitrary information later in the day.","Violet is the Poisoner bluffing as the Egotist. They are nominated by the Clockmaker, and the claimed Fortune Teller votes on their execution. After surviving, at night, Violet poisons the Fortune Teller."],"firstNight":0,"firstNightReminder":"","otherNight":0,"otherNightReminder":"","reminders":["Drunk"],"setup":false,"image":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/egog.png","curata":false,"imageAlt":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/egoe.png"}','published','the-menagerie/egotist',datetime('now'),datetime('now')),
('fixer','Fixer','outsider','Goodpart',NULL,NULL,'The Menagerie','{"slug":"fixer","name":"Fixer","team":"outsider","ability":"On your first night, choose 3 players (not yourself). If 2 are among the last 3 alive, you win with the winning team, even if dead. If any die, you might die at any time.","creator":"Goodpart","appearsIn":"The Menagerie","quote":"Now listen here, bub. I''ve got five hundred bones on Morozov over there, so no funny stuff. Stick to the plan, and make sure he makes it out alive. If he goes down, we all go down. You get me?","lede":"The Fixer places their bets and wins no matter what - or else.","howToRun":["Remember to change the Fixer''s alignment to that of the winning team, should the Fixer meet its criteria."],"tips":["Like the Politician, you get to choose which side you play for - but unlike the Politician, who can change on a dime depending on which team is winning, the Fixer has to make their choice at the start of the game. So don''t back down from defending your chosen players, and make sure at least two of them make it to the very end. If one dies along the way, it''s no big deal, but given that you might die at any time, you''ll ultimately be a thorn in the good team''s side, as it will cause confusion as to what may have caused your exit. All is not lost should your chosen players not quite make it, since, as a good player, you still adhere to the same win conditions as the good team. You have two shots at winning, which is great - it just may not be entirely helpful, especially if you''ve accidentally chosen an all evil trio!"],"bluffing":["Are you feeling called out for defending players who may not necessarily gel with town''s information? No problem! You''re the Fixer - and you''re just playing to your ability. The Fixer gives evil players a viable reason for taking certain positions on certain players, which means you can vote irregularly, nominate players outside of your \"chosen three\", and generally be a nuisance to the good team. Consider including a good player among the three just for credibility, as you don''t want to point directly to your team - but also note that should any of them die, you''ll be expected to die suddenly as well. Don''t worry, you say, it''s just a \"might\"."],"fighting":[],"examples":["David is the Fixer. He selects the Washerwoman, Shabaloth and Colossus on Night 1. The Washerwoman is executed on the first day, and David dies along with that night''s kill on Night 4. The Shabaloth and Colossus ultimately make it to the final 3, and David doesn''t care what happens next, because no matter who wins, David wins.","Isabella is the Godfather bluffing as the Fixer. She takes up a staunch defense of the Fang Gu, the Drunk, and the Pacifist. The Drunk is executed on Day 3, and Isabella chooses herself with her ability, suggesting she died to the Fixer''s ability, and not the Godfather''s."],"firstNight":47,"firstNightReminder":"The Fixer chooses 3 players.","otherNight":0,"otherNightReminder":"","reminders":["Bet","Bet","Bet","Dead"],"setup":false,"image":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/doubg.png","curata":false,"imageAlt":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/doube.png"}','published','the-menagerie/fixer',datetime('now'),datetime('now')),
('missionary','Missionary','outsider','Goodpart',NULL,NULL,'The Menagerie','{"slug":"missionary","name":"Missionary","team":"outsider","ability":"You must ask the player you wish to nominate for permission. If you nominate without permission, you might die tonight.","creator":"Goodpart","appearsIn":"The Menagerie","quote":"Hello there! Could you spare a moment to learn about our lord and-- ah, of course, have a nice day.","lede":"The Missionary risks death if they nominate without the permission of the person they are nominating.","howToRun":["Note that the Missionary is not prone to death unless they specifically nominate a player without asking permission, or if permission is not granted. Consider not killing them in case there is suspicion around them, else you risk confirming them."],"tips":["Always say please and thank you.","You may want to nominate without permission in order to confirm your identity, as a Mutant might, but this isn''t a guarantee, so just be nice. It takes more muscles to frown than it does to smile."],"bluffing":["No, seriously, always say please and thank you.","This is a straightforward bluff, in that you simply have to follow the golden rule of the Missionary. If you do, there is little reason for town to suspect you - but if there is an opportunity for a double kill, you may want to consider nominating out of turn to confirm yourself, assuming you are expendable at that point in the game."],"fighting":[],"examples":["Sarah is the Missionary. They request permission from the Mayor before nominating, and the Mayor says no. The Missionary nominates them anyway, and they die during the night.","Sean is the Assassin bluffing as the Missionary. They nominate the Fortune Teller without asking permission. That night, the Assassin selects themselves, resulting in two deaths overnight."],"firstNight":0,"firstNightReminder":"","otherNight":0,"otherNightReminder":"","reminders":[],"setup":false,"image":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/misg.png","curata":false,"imageAlt":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/mise.png"}','published','the-menagerie/missionary',datetime('now'),datetime('now')),
('oaf','Oaf','outsider','Goodpart',NULL,NULL,'The Menagerie','{"slug":"oaf","name":"Oaf","team":"outsider","ability":"If a non-Demon ability would target you, it might target a living neighbour instead. If targeted 3 times, lose your ability & die at night.","creator":"Goodpart","appearsIn":"The Menagerie","quote":"Uh oh. Sorry. Uh ohhhhh. Sorryyyyy.","lede":"The Oaf''s clumsy nature causes misinformation to spread, and might one day kill them.","howToRun":["This is an Outsider ability, and thus should be harmful to town. Only bounce abilities should it be beneficial to the evil team - though you can always temper the potency of this effect by targeting the Oaf instead. This is a useful tool if evil is doing particularly well. You may also do this if doing otherwise would risk confirmation of other players."],"tips":["Let your neighbours know they''re in for a rough ride! As the Oaf, you are liable to have abilities bounce off you, meaning that there is a possibility for errant information to spread from Fortune Tellers, Dreamers, or even Minions. The only upside is that once targeted enough, the Oaf simply can''t take it anymore and dies in the night. This may serve as some measure of confirmation, but unfortunately you''ve accelerated the game, and not in a good way.","You can engineer your ability such that by learning about your neighbours, you can ask Townsfolk to target you with their abilities, burning up your own ability and ensuring that information is (reasonably) reliable. No guarantees, of course.","You also have the benefit of being a fairly confirmable Outsider: there aren’t many ways you can cause an extra death at night, but of course, if you’ve been too public about your role, you can always be targeted and killed in the same night - so be judicious with who you tell.","And if a Gambler ever asks to pick you in the night, or if a Golem asks to nominate you, or if a Moonchild wants to point at you… no thanks."],"bluffing":["As with a role like the Tinker, bluffing as the Oaf is easy, right up until it’s not. People will begin to question why you are still alive, especially if you’ve been targeted by multiple abilities, but if you’re a Minion who can afford to be caught out, this isn’t so bad - but planning your escape route ensures the information you’ve “corrupted” remains relevant to your neighbours instead. Consider covering your tracks with other Minions like the Godfather or Assassin, or Demons like the Polterghast or Zombuul!","Unlike the Tinker who can die at any time per the Storyteller’s discretion, there is a hard cap on how many times an Oaf can impact the game before they’re spent, so keep track of who is targeting you, and do your best to frame your neighbours that way.","If you think an Oaf is in play, why not kill them early on a night when you have a second kill to spare? Doing so will imply that the Oaf has bounced far more than previously believed, causing other players to doubt their information if nearby."],"fighting":[],"examples":["Tom is the Oaf. He is targeted by the Fortune Teller along with another player, and it bounces to a neighbour: the Red Herring. The same night, Tom is targeted by the Cerenovus, causing Tom''s other neighbour to be made mad. The night after, Tom is chosen by the Monk: the Monk protection does not bounce, but Tom dies anyway.","Bert is the Imp bluffing as the Oaf. On a night after an Outsider was executed, they pass to their Scarlet Woman, and the Godfather kills another player."],"firstNight":0,"firstNightReminder":"","otherNight":70,"otherNightReminder":"If the Oaf has been targeted by 3 abilities in total thus far, they die.","reminders":["Bounced 1","Bounced 2","Bounced 3","Dies Tonight"],"setup":false,"jinxes":[{"name":"Saboteur","align":"good","text":"The Saboteur can redirect abilities from - but not to - the Oaf without triggering its ability.","slug":"saboteur-the-menagerie"}],"image":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/oafg.png","curata":false,"imageAlt":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/oafe.png"}','published','the-menagerie/oaf',datetime('now'),datetime('now')),
('record-keeper','Record Keeper','outsider','Goodpart',NULL,NULL,'The Menagerie','{"slug":"record-keeper","name":"Record Keeper","team":"outsider","ability":"If you are executed, the Demon sees the Grimoire tonight.","creator":"Goodpart","appearsIn":"The Menagerie","quote":"You would be surprised as to what people are capable of when they think nobody is watching.","lede":"The Record Keeper carries the Grimoire wherever they go, and doesn''t want it to fall into the wrong hands.","howToRun":["Remember to show the Grimoire to the Demon at the appropriate point in the night order so that information is provided per what the Demon would see when the Record Keeper is up in the night order."],"tips":["Stay alive! Although you start with knowledge about the game, be careful about who you share that information with, or simply use it to sniff out trusted allies: your death can have disastrous consequences for the good team. Consider bluffing a powerful role in order to ensure the Demon kills you at night – especially if it’s one you learn. But take care not to accidentally find yourself on the wrong end of a double claim, as this might lead to your execution."],"bluffing":["No Record Keeper ever wants their wares to fall into the wrong hands via execution, so act like it. Putting you on the block is a terrible idea! Like the Saint, you can push for a world where you must stay alive, and ask that town leaves it to the Demon to dispatch you. As such, you can avoid execution day after day and find yourself alive and healthy when it counts. Consider coordinating with fellow Minions like the Godfather, or lean into confirming other bluffs in order to fill out your known roles. You may even out which Demon is in play to lend yourself further credibility."],"fighting":[],"examples":["Rhona is the Record Keeper. Rhona is executed on Day 4, and the Demon sees the Grimoire that night.","Minh is the Vortox bluffing as the Record Keeper. Minh is never executed. Great job, Minh."],"firstNight":0,"firstNightReminder":"","otherNight":29,"otherNightReminder":"If the Record Keeper has died by execution today, show the Demon the Grimoire.","reminders":["Executed"],"setup":false,"special":[{"type":"signal","name":"grimoire","time":"night","global":"demon"}],"jinxes":[{"name":"Damsel","align":"good","text":"If a Damsel is in play, they are drunk when the Record Keeper dies.","id":"damsel"},{"name":"Poppy Grower","align":"good","text":"If the Poppy Grower is in play and the Record Keeper dies, the Demon does not see the Grimoire until the Poppy Grower dies.","id":"poppygrower"}],"image":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/recg.png","curata":false,"imageAlt":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/rece.png"}','published','the-menagerie/record-keeper',datetime('now'),datetime('now')),
('snoop-the-menagerie','Snoop','outsider','Goodpart',NULL,NULL,'The Menagerie','{"slug":"snoop-the-menagerie","name":"Snoop","team":"outsider","ability":"You start knowing a neighbour''s character (Travellers don''t count); if they are evil, info you receive is arbitrary. The Demon starts knowing the player and character of the other neighbour.","creator":"Goodpart","appearsIn":"The Menagerie","quote":"I''ve always wondered what''s behind this door--","lede":"The Snoop sees one of its neighbours, but gives the Demon a look as well.","howToRun":["The Snoop is an Outsider, so consider giving them the less powerful of the two available roles, opting to provide the Demon with the more powerful one.","Additionally, if the Snoop neighbours an evil player, ensure that the role you give is in fact one of the bluffs - or, if possible, an out-of-play role entirely, to give that Minion or Demon something extra to bluff."],"tips":["It''s not often that an Outsider gets information, but sadly, your sneaky ways have let the Demon in on a few secrets of their own. Consider trying to confirm the neighbour you see, as that can form a powerful confirmation chain, but remember that evil players will be seen as good roles regardless - so while you may be confirming a good player, you may instead be giving a free bluff to an evil player! There''s nothing wrong with withholding your information, but as a courtesy, it might be useful to let your other neighbour know that the Demon knows precisely who they are."],"bluffing":["Want to coax a hard claim out of a neighbour? Bluffing as the Snoop might be just the thing! Telling a neighbour that they''ve been \"seen\" by the Demon might push them to claim their role and even out themselves to town, making them a prime target at night, as long as they''re telling the truth. Consider trying to confirm your other neighbour as soon as is reasonable, since people may doubt you are what you claim if you''re unable to produce a role in a timely fashion.","Alternatively, you may want to confront a neighbour with a role you know they aren''t, in an effort to frame them as evil. They know you''re either poisoned or lying, but who''s to say who''s correct?"],"fighting":[],"examples":["Maggie is the Snoop. On Night 1, she sees that one of her neighbours is the Artist. The Demon has seen that Maggie''s other neighbour is the Fortune Teller. Maggie confronts her neighbour with this information, and offers her condolences to her other neighbour. Sorry about that.","Cal is the Boffin bluffing as the Snoop. He immediately informs one of his neighbours that the Demon has seen them, and they out to Cal as the Slayer. They pressure the Slayer into shooting that day, ultimately wasting their shot, since the Demon is primed to kill them that night."],"firstNight":30,"firstNightReminder":"Show the Snoop a neighbour''s character, or any good character if evil. Wake the Demon and show them that THIS PLAYER IS and their corresponding character.","otherNight":0,"otherNightReminder":"","reminders":[],"setup":false,"image":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/snog.png","curata":false,"imageAlt":"https://menagerie.towerrangers.net/images/snoe.png"}','published','the-menagerie/snoop',datetime('now'),datetime('now'));